# Testing: cloud first

Several agents work on this machine at once, and none sees the others. Parallel vitest and tsc runs make it unusable,
so the suites run on Modal through the shared cloud test runner (the same one br-motor-builder uses), set by the user
on 2026-10-24.

The runner is the `run.mjs` named in the user's global cloud-tests rule (`~/.claude/rules/cloud-tests.md`); its README has the flags,
sizing, exit codes and costs. It packs the working tree as it is, uncommitted edits included, and picks Node 22 from
`engines.node`.

| local command | cloud command (`$run` = the runner path above) |
|---|---|
| focused `npx vitest run <files>` | `node $run --repo . --gate vitest --paths <a.test.ts> [more] --timeout-min 10` |
| `npm run test` | `node $run --repo . --gate test --cores 16 --timeout-min 20` |
| `npm run typecheck` | `node $run --repo . --gate check --cores 16 --timeout-min 15` (runs `npm run check:all`) |

- `--cores 16` on purpose: the runner defaults full runs to 64 cores, which pays off for br-motor-builder but not here.
  bluePLM's suite is about 170 CPU-seconds, so 64 cores saved 4 s on the test step at about 7x the cost (measured
  2026-10-24, runner README).
- Exit 0 is a pass; a failing gate passes its own exit code through. A failure is a result: never rerun it locally.
- Local is the backup only when the runner is missing, Modal is unreachable (exit 2), the run failed as
  infrastructure (exit 4) or the spend cap refused it. Then run one command at a time, never alongside another test
  or tsc process, and say in the report that it was a local backup run and why.
- `npm run typecheck:api` stays local: `api/` has its own `package.json`, and the runner installs only the root
  dependencies. It is a single tsc over `api/`, a few seconds.
- `npm run lint` is cheap enough to run locally on the files you changed (`npx eslint <files>`).
- The spend cap is `tools/cloud-test/CAP.txt` and the ledger `SPEND.md` beside it. `run.mjs` writes the ledger; nobody
  edits its rows.
- The container is Linux: paths are case-sensitive and the time zone is UTC. A test that passes on Windows and fails
  there is usually one of those.
- Before a tag, `npm run typecheck` must pass (see `always.mdc`); the `check` gate covers it.
